                <pb facs="0750" n="726" xml:id="pg726"/>

                <head>349. Memorandum for the Files<anchor n="0" xml:id="d349-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-05-09">May 9,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Luncheon Conversation between the Attorney General and Ambassador Dobrynin
                        on May 9, 1962</item>
                </list>
                <p>The Attorney General lunched today with Ambassador Dobrynin, who had the
                    following comments to make on the situation in Laos: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>It is unfortunate that the United States has taken so long to move the
                            RLG to negotiations on a coalition government.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Nam Tha is an understandable event in the light of Phoumi’s recently
                            sending additional battalions there.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>It is unfortunate that this has happened; but Premier Khrushchev has
                            not changed his policy of achieving an independent and neutral
                            Laos.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
